---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Our Approach | Cassady Tech Solutions";
const description = "Meet Cassady Tech Solutions and learn how we approach assessments, projects, cybersecurity, advisory work, and responsible modernization for small organizations.";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} active="about">
	<section class="page-title page-title-paper">
		<div class="section-inner page-title-grid">
			<div><p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p><h1>Useful technology starts with paying attention.</h1><p>Cassady Tech Solutions was built around a simple observation: small organizations often carry serious technology responsibility without enough context, time, or internal ownership.</p></div>
			<div class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section founder-section">
		<div class="section-inner founder-grid">
			<div class="founder-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2>Sometimes an organization needs a good technology partner more than it needs a full IT department.</h2><p>Sam Cassady built Cassady Tech Solutions to help organizations close the gap between “we have technology” and “we understand what we depend on and what to do next.” The work draws on professional cybersecurity analysis, IT administration, military leadership, and hands-on support for real people with real constraints.</p><p>That background shapes the way we work: understand the problem, make the scope clear, stabilize what matters, improve what is worth improving, and be honest about what the organization actually needs afterward.</p></div>
			<aside class="founder-card"><div class="founder-card-top"><span>FOUNDER / PRINCIPAL</span><span class="card-index">SAM</span></div><h3>Sam Cassady</h3><p>Cybersecurity analyst<br />Master's degree in cybersecurity<br />CompTIA Security+ certified<br />U.S. military veteran</p><div class="founder-card-rule"></div><p class="small">Based in Southern Colorado. Working with local organizations and remote-first teams.</p></aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section alt-section principles-section">
		<div class="section-inner">
			<div class="section-heading wide-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Working principles</p><h2>How we try to leave things.</h2></div>
			<div class="principle-grid">
				<article><span>01</span><h3>Clearer than before</h3><p>A useful engagement should improve the system and the organization's understanding of it.</p></article>
				<article><span>02</span><h3>Proportionate to the risk</h3><p>Security and resilience matter, but the answer still has to fit the environment and the people maintaining it.</p></article>
				<article><span>03</span><h3>Bounded where possible</h3><p>Clear outcomes, scope, and ownership make projects easier to deliver well and easier for customers to understand.</p></article>
				<article><span>04</span><h3>Honest about the relationship</h3><p>Some customers need a project. Some need periodic advice. Some eventually need ongoing management. We do not treat those as the same sale.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section brand-relationship-section">
		<div class="section-inner brand-relationship-grid">
			<div><p class="eyebrow">One company, two kinds of relationship</p><h2>Community technology help and organizational responsibility should not feel identical.</h2><p>Greenhorn Valley Tech is the local relationship for people, homes, and community technology needs. Cassady Tech Solutions is the organizational technology layer for teams that need someone to assess, fix, plan, implement, advise, or take responsibility for a defined business technology problem.</p></div>
			<div class="brand-pair"><a href="https://ghvtech.com"><span class="brand-pair-label">Greenhorn Valley Tech</span><strong>Technology for people and homes</strong><span>Local device, Wi-Fi, account, and digital safety help.</span></a><div class="pair-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="brand-pair current"><span class="brand-pair-label">Cassady Tech Solutions</span><strong>Technology for organizations</strong><span>Assessments, projects, security, advisory, automation, and AI enablement.</span></div></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band"><div class="section-inner band-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">No pitch deck required</p><h2>Bring the messy version of the problem.</h2><p>We will help turn it into a clearer technology decision and a useful next piece of work.</p></div><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Talk with Cassady Tech</a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
